<div class="mb-requirement-container">
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16311">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> </span>
      <b>NOTE: </b> Check out the Digital Resource Guide for the Wildland Fire
      Management merit badge
      <a
        href="https://www.scouting.org/skills/merit-badges/digital-resource-guides/wildland-fire-management/"
        target="_blank"
        >HERE</a
      >
      for detailed information and helpful resources to engage your learning and
      assist you along on your merit badge journey!
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16312">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 1. </span>
      <b>History of Wildland Fire.</b> Research and discuss with your counselor
      the history of wildland fire, its suppression, prevention, and management
      in the United States. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
      <a href="https://youtu.be/ZnabcDAQ1DU" target="_blank"
        >A History of Wildfire Prevention (video)</a
      ><br />
      <a
        href="https://www.nifc.gov/fire-information/fire-prevention-education-mitigation/wildfire-education"
        target="_blank"
        >Wildfire Education (website)</a
      >
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16313">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 2. </span>
      <b>Harms of Wildfire.</b> Research the harm caused by wildfire in the
      United States, including annual acres burned for the past three years.
      Discuss with your counselor. Include the negative impacts that wildfire
      has on the following: <br /><i>Resources:</i>
      <a href="https://youtu.be/HeOl2N6iLy0" target="_blank"
        >A Better Way To Think About Wildland Fires (video)</a
      ><br />
      <a href="https://youtu.be/bmX4kxdSi98" target="_blank"
        >Effects of Wildfires and Forest Fires (video)</a
      >
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16313 mb-requirement-id-16314">
        (a) Commercial forest products
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16313 mb-requirement-id-16315">
        (b) Fish and wildlife habitat <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/P5EoR12vHcQ" target="_blank"
          >The Impact of Wildfires on Wildlife (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16313 mb-requirement-id-16316">
        (c) Soil and water <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/RV_OZ430GAs" target="_blank"
          >How Wildfires Affect Water Supply (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16313 mb-requirement-id-16317">
        (d) Recreation and public use
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16313 mb-requirement-id-16318">
        (e) Homes, communities, and human resources
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16313 mb-requirement-id-16319">
        (f) Air quality and public health <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/8mQllQnJrhg" target="_blank"
          >How Are Wildfires Making Us Sick? (video)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16320">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 3. </span>
      <b>Fire as a Management Tool.</b> Discuss with your counselor how
      prescribed fire is used to accomplish the following: <br /><i
        >Resource:</i
      >
      <a href="https://youtu.be/vFPIoH4ML2U" target="_blank"
        >Misconceptions and Benefits of Fire (video)</a
      >
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16320 mb-requirement-id-16321">
        (a) Fuel reduction <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/E542gY7uR0s" target="_blank"
          >Good Fire: Prescribed Burning (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16320 mb-requirement-id-16322">
        (b) Fish and wildlife habitat enhancement <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/Q8mD-4rexo0" target="_blank"
          >Wildlife That Depends on Fire To Survive (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16320 mb-requirement-id-16323">
        (c) Ecosystem restoration <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/iKRYDp6VpyA" target="_blank"
          >How Does Fire Affect Wildlife? (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16320 mb-requirement-id-16324">
        (d) Forest regeneration <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/BxKh86ukZMc" target="_blank"
          >Fire Effects in the Forest (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16320 mb-requirement-id-16325">
        (e) Insect and disease control <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/e_cOMAioE54" target="_blank"
          >Insects, Disease, Drought, and Fire (video)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16326">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 4. </span>
      <b>Wildfire Prevention and Mitigation.</b> Discuss the following with your
      counselor:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16326 mb-requirement-id-16327">
        (a) Wildfire Prevention:<br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://www.usfa.fema.gov/prevention/fief/" target="_blank"
          >Fire Is Everyone's Fight (website)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16327 mb-requirement-id-16328">
        (1) The main causes of wildfire in the United States <br /><i
          >Resource:</i
        >
        <a href="https://youtu.be/5hghT1W33cY" target="_blank"
          >Wildfires 101 (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16327 mb-requirement-id-16329">
        (2) How you can prevent human caused wildfires in your community and on
        outings with your unit. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/tUTyDGlJt00" target="_blank"
          >Wildfire Prevention With Smokey the Bear (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16326 mb-requirement-id-16330">
        (b) Wildfire Mitigation:
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16330 mb-requirement-id-16331">
        (1) Wildland-Urban Interface <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a
          href="https://storymaps.arcgis.com/stories/6b2050a0ded0498c863ce30d73460c9e"
          target="_blank"
          >Understanding the Wildland Urban Interface (website)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16330 mb-requirement-id-16332">
        (2) Defensible space and how homes and communities in the wildland-urban
        interface can be protected from wildfire <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/isf6COwOXPw" target="_blank"
          >Separating Your Home From Wildfire—the Zones of Defensible Space
          (video)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16333">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 5. </span>
      <b>Fire Behavior. </b>Do the following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16333 mb-requirement-id-16334">
        (a) Discuss with your counselor how the fire environment affects
        wildland fire behavior. Include examples of the influences of weather,
        topography, and fuel. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/FUdPfKL8lXA" target="_blank"
          >The Relationship Between Relative Humidity, Fuel Moisture, and Fire
          Behavior (video)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://www.nps.gov/articles/wildland-fire-behavior.htm"
          target="_blank"
          >Wildland Fire Behavior (website)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16333 mb-requirement-id-16335">
        (b) Explain how a wildfire can be suppressed by removing heat, fuel, or
        oxygen. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/8WPk15XqN2E" target="_blank"
          >Fire Triangle Explained (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16333 mb-requirement-id-16336">
        (c) Draw a diagram to illustrate the parts of a wildfire. <br /><i
          >Resource:</i
        >
        <a href="https://youtu.be/b1KvTswZYNA" target="_blank"
          >How To Describe the Behavior and Parts of a Wildfire (video)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16337">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 6. </span>
      <b>Wildland Firefighter Safety.</b> Do the following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16337 mb-requirement-id-16338">
        (a) Discuss with your counselor the personal protective equipment used
        by wildland firefighters and its use. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/a0NtIJMDUD4" target="_blank"
          >Dressed for Fire (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16337 mb-requirement-id-16339">
        (b) Discuss the following with your counselor, including why each is an
        important consideration for maintaining personal safety and situational
        awareness during wildland fire suppression activities:
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16339 mb-requirement-id-16340">
        (1) 10 Standard Firefighting Orders <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/9WhKKSGl9K0" target="_blank"
          >Standard Firefighting Orders (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16339 mb-requirement-id-16341">
        (2) 18 Watch Out Situations <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/GIMeOZ_d1ko" target="_blank"
          >The Watchout Situations (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16339 mb-requirement-id-16342">
        (3) Lookouts, Communication, Escape Routes, and Safety Zones (LCES)
        <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/46kiCPcfUyg" target="_blank">LCES (video)</a>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16343">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 7. </span>
      <b>Wildfire Suppression Tactics.</b> Do the following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16343 mb-requirement-id-16344">
        (a) Alone or with a small team, using the diagram you created in
        Requirement 5(c) or a map of a wildfire, and tokens to represent
        firefighting resources, demonstrate the following wildland fire
        suppression tactics. Explain under which conditions each tactic would be
        used: <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/9EzcA3KvEsY" target="_blank"
          >How We Fight Wildfires (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16344 mb-requirement-id-16345">
        (1) Direct attack <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/HDmGToDhgV4" target="_blank"
          >Direct and Indirect Attack Strategies on Wildfires (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16344 mb-requirement-id-16346">
        (2) Indirect attack
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16344 mb-requirement-id-16347">
        (3) Minimum impact suppression tactics <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/W8GHIZAaUaQ" target="_blank"
          >Evolution of Fire Management and the Role of Knowledge (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16344 mb-requirement-id-16348">
        (4) Use of hand crews, machinery, and aircraft <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/Dw0wY6SgG2w" target="_blank"
          >California Battles Fires With "Fire Plane" (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16344 mb-requirement-id-16349">
        (5) Mop-up <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/DNFv_cr8r7I" target="_blank"
          >Mop Up Operations on the Mosquito Fire (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16344 mb-requirement-id-16350">
        (6) Repair and restoration
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16343 mb-requirement-id-16351">
        (b) Draw a diagram of the Incident Command System. Alone or with your
        team, explain the responsibilities of the Command and General Staff
        positions on a wildfire incident. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a
          href="https://training.fema.gov/emiweb/is/icsresource/assets/ics%20organizational%20structure%20and%20elements.pdf"
          target="_blank"
          >ICS Organizational Structure and Elements (PDF)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16352">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 8. </span>
      <b>Wildfire Suppression Tools.</b> Do the following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16352 mb-requirement-id-16353">
        (a) Demonstrate the use of three hand tools unique to wildland fire
        suppression. Use one of these tools to demonstrate how to construct a
        fireline. <br /><i>Resource:</i>
        <a href="https://youtu.be/SHXLUEfHlxw" target="_blank"
          >Wildland Firefighting Tools (video)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16352 mb-requirement-id-16354">
        (b) Discuss seven other tools, equipment, or apparatus that are unique
        to wildland fire suppression and explain how these resources are used.
        <br /><i>Resources:</i>
        <a
          href="https://www.nps.gov/articles/wildland-fire-engines.htm"
          target="_blank"
          >Wildland Fire Engines (website w/ video)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://www.nifc.gov/resources/aircraft" target="_blank"
          >Aircraft (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a href="https://www.nifc.gov/resources/equipment" target="_blank"
          >Firefighting Equipment (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://www.nifc.gov/resources/equipment/dozers"
          target="_blank"
          >Dozers (website)</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16355">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 9. </span>
      <b>Taking Action.</b> Do ONE of the following:
    </div>
    <ul class="mb-requirement-children-list">
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16355 mb-requirement-id-16356">
        (a) Develop a fire readiness plan for a wildland area with which you are
        familiar. The plan should include a map showing available resources,
        water supplies, natural and manmade barriers, and access. The plan
        should discuss fuel loads, available fire apparatus, structure
        protection needs, values at risk, medical and evacuation considerations
        and potential fire suppression tactics.
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16355 mb-requirement-id-16357">
        (b) Visit with a state or federal forestry official or your local fire
        warden. Discuss the causes of and types of wildland fire that occur in
        your area. Discuss the prime fire season(s) in your area. Identify the
        agency responsible for wildland fire suppression in your area. Discuss
        what you learned with your counselor.
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16355 mb-requirement-id-16358">
        (c) Conduct a Firewise assessment of a home or a building in the
        wildland-urban interface, which could include a Scout camp building or
        facility. Identify potential risks and fire hazards. With your
        counselor's approval, complete a project to reduce the wildfire risk and
        increase the preparedness of the building. Write a brief report about
        what you did and learned from the assessment and project. <br /><i
          >Resources:</i
        >
        <a
          href="https://www.nfpa.org/en/education-and-research/wildfire/preparing-homes-for-wildfire"
          target="_blank"
          >Firewise USA® (website)</a
        ><br />
        <a
          href="https://dem.ri.gov/sites/g/files/xkgbur861/files/programs/bnatres/forest/pdf/fire/fire-home-assessment-form.pdf"
          target="_blank"
          >Fire Home Assessment (PDF)</a
        >
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16355 mb-requirement-id-16359">
        (d) Meet with a Fire Prevention Specialist or a local fire official to
        learn about fire prevention efforts in your community. From what you
        learned, prepare a fire prevention message (skit, video, or billboard
        concept) and share with your counselor and troop (or other group
        approved by your counselor).
      </li>
      <li class="mb-requirement-child mb-parent-16355 mb-requirement-id-16360">
        (e) Meet with a meteorologist or someone familiar with fire weather and
        discuss the fire weather concerns and typical fire seasons that exist in
        your area. Discuss the conditions that lead to a Fire Weather Watch or a
        Red Flag Warning. Discuss what you learned with your counselor.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div style="padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: #515354"></div>
    <br />
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16361">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 10. </span>
      <b>Apply Your Learning to a Real Event.</b> Research an historic
      catastrophic wildland fire incident that occurred in the United States.
      Discuss with your counselor and/or your troop or a group approved by your
      counselor the conditions that led to the incident, how the incident was
      managed, and how the incident could have been prevented. Explain what
      lessons were learned and how this incident affected future fire
      suppression policy or suppression tactics. <br /><i>Resources:</i>
      <a href="https://youtu.be/LatzdMh49ps" target="_blank"
        >The Tillamook Burn Forest Fire of August, 1933 (video)</a
      ><br />
      <a href="https://youtu.be/CAgP9fo3f7s" target="_blank"
        >The Story Behind the Yellowstone Fires of 1988 (video)</a
      ><br />
      <a href="https://youtu.be/uKJdfYijVvQ" target="_blank"
        >The Smoke Jumper Tragedy of Mann Gulch (video)</a
      ><br />
      <a href="https://youtu.be/7UVaFKnN-gI" target="_blank"
        >Storm King Mountain Tragedy (video)</a
      >
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mb-requirement-item">
    <div class="mb-requirement-parent mb-requirement-id-16362">
      <span class="mb-requirement-listnumber"> 11. </span>
      <b>Careers in Wildland Fire Management.</b> Explore careers related to
      this merit badge. Research one career to learn about the training and
      education needed, costs, job prospects, salary, job duties, and career
      advancement. Your research methods may include-with your parent or
      guardian's permission-an internet or library search, an interview with a
      professional in the field, or a visit to a location where people in this
      career work. Discuss with your counselor both your findings and what about
      this profession might make it an interesting career. <br /><i
        >Resources:</i
      >
      <a href="https://youtu.be/55iglSp3ki0" target="_blank"
        >Wildland Firefighting &amp; Wildland Fire Ecology Jobs (video)</a
      ><br />
      <a
        href="https://careers.iafc.org/career/fire-management-specialist"
        target="_blank"
        >Fire Management Specialist (website)</a
      ><br />
      <a href="https://youtu.be/ewR1Ryqvr2Y" target="_blank"
        >The Forest Service's Wildfire Force (video)</a
      >
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
